{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "comment": "X-02 \u00a72, \u00a76.1-\u00a76.3 (rev 14). 'fetch': tls.fetch's tagged result, {ok:{mode:https,cert,key,origin,hsts}} | {ok:{mode:http_loopback,origin,hsts}} | {unavailable:ListenFailure}; 'expect' is the decoded form or 'refused'. Accepted rows serialize back to the same JSON. 'listen_failure' is ListenFailure alone (status, doctor and unavailable): {reason:origin_invalid} | {reason:hsts_invalid} | {reason:tls_name_mismatch,uncovered:[canonical origins]}. 'refusals': the tls.set/bootstrap refusals with their wire forms and whether each op journals them (only tls.set's tls_key_mismatch; no bootstrap refusal is ever stored). 'bad_refusals' don't decode. 'listen_config': the invalid-configuration rule on a stored listen configuration; 'result' is 'valid', 'origin_invalid' (with the OriginError code) or 'hsts_invalid', which the host reports as that ListenFailure and bootstrap and tls.set refuse with as that code. A missing origin or hsts has no default. 'bootstrap': bootstrap's HostOpResult, never 'accepted': completed {result:{session}} or rejected {refusal}, the refusal a TlsRefusal or {code:tls_required} / {code:tls_mismatch}; 'expect' is 'completed', the refusal's code, or 'refused'. No bootstrap refusal is ever stored.",
  "fetch": [
    {
      "name": "https serves the stored pair with the snapshot's origin and hsts",
      "wire": {
        "ok": {
          "mode": "https",
          "cert": "-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\nMIIB...\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\n",
          "key": "-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nsecret-key-material\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n",
          "origin": "https://mac.local:8443",
          "hsts": "on"
        }
      },
      "expect": "https"
    },
    {
      "name": "https on the default port",
      "wire": {
        "ok": {
          "mode": "https",
          "cert": "-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\nMIIB...\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\n",
          "key": "-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nsecret-key-material\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n",
          "origin": "https://mac.local",
          "hsts": "clear"
        }
      },
      "expect": "https"
    },
    {
      "name": "http_loopback carries no certificate fields",
      "wire": {
        "ok": {
          "mode": "http_loopback",
          "origin": "http://127.0.0.1:8080",
          "hsts": "off"
        }
      },
      "expect": "http_loopback"
    },
    {
      "name": "http_loopback on ::1",
      "wire": {
        "ok": {
          "mode": "http_loopback",
          "origin": "http://[::1]:8080",
          "hsts": "off"
        }
      },
      "expect": "http_loopback"
    },
    {
      "name": "unavailable: origin_invalid",
